{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## THE SEAM IS UP — Gerrit 1329. Read what it does and does NOT change carefully.\n\n`_diff_comments` now composes its local comparison key as\n`codec.normalize_outbound(sanitizer.fit_comment(body))` — **fit-then-normalize, the same order\n`outbound_mapper.map_fields_to_remote` uses for descriptions.** Injected via a `codec` parameter\nmirroring the existing `_resolve_inbound_mapper` / `_resolve_sanitizer` seam.\n\n### PRODUCTION BEHAVIOUR IS UNCHANGED TODAY, and that is deliberate — but be precise about it\n\nThe parameter defaults to `_IdentityCodec`, and **nothing wires a real codec into\n`compute_outbound_mutations`** — verified: `grep codec outbound_differ.py` returns nothing. So the\nkey reduces to exactly `sanitizer.fit_comment(body)`, today's existing formula. Every existing\nprotection (truncation guard, marker strip, whitespace strip) behaves byte-identically.\n\nThat is the right scope *now*, and the reason is worth stating: rebar applies NO content\ntransformation on the comment send path — Cloud comments go out through ACLI as\n`--body <text>` and ACLI's own conversion is opaque to us; DC's `WikiTextCodec` is pure identity.\nThere is no real codec to inject yet. **So AC1 is met STRUCTURALLY — the key now routes through the\ncodec seam — but the latent bug is DISARMED BY CONSTRUCTION rather than fixed-and-proven.** When\npandoc or any Markdown-aware encoder lands, injecting the real codec is a one-line change and the\nnew cells prove it converges.\n\nDo not read this ticket as \"comment dedup is now correct under conversion\". Read it as \"the seam and\nthe proof exist, so conversion can land without re-discovering this\".\n\n### The convergence argument, which is the part that matters\n\nThe Jira-side key was and remains `decode_inbound(<wire body>)`. The local key is now\n`normalize_outbound(fit(local))`. The codec law `normalize_outbound(t) == decode_inbound(to_wire(t))`\n— **now PINNED by a new test for BOTH `AdfCodec` and `WikiTextCodec`** — makes those equal once a\nreal codec is wired into a send path where `to_wire(fit(local))` is what Jira stores. Same\nfixed-point argument that already protects descriptions.\n\n### Evidence\n\nRED first, verbatim: 8 of 9 new cells failed with\n`TypeError: _diff_comments() got an unexpected keyword argument 'codec'`. The ninth passed by\ndesign — the \"no codec injected, baseline unchanged\" negative control, which needed no new code and\nis what proves the default path is untouched.\n\nThe missing cell now exists and uses the REAL `AdfCodec`, not a stub: a non-identity codec plus an\nalready-mirrored comment must emit ZERO adds. Plus the counter-regression (a genuinely new comment\nis still emitted — the too-lax direction), and an idempotence property over soft-wrapped prose, code\nfences, bullets, emphasis, literal pipes and backticks.\n\nGates: ruff clean, mypy 421, hygiene 0, **2161 passed** across unit + integration.\n`outbound_comments.py` 407/800.\n\n### A NEAR-MISS WORTH RECORDING\n\nThe implementer's editing tool was briefly pointed at the SHARED main checkout\n(`/Users/joeoakhart/rebar`) instead of its isolated worktree — the checkout AGENTS.md and\nCLAUDE.local.md single out as possibly holding uncommitted operator WIP. It caught this itself\nbefore running anything and restored the file.\n\n**I verified the restore independently rather than accepting the report**: `git status --short` in\nthat checkout is EMPTY, `outbound_comments.py` is byte-identical to HEAD, and no stray test file\nexists. Nothing was lost. But it was clean only because there happened to be no WIP there at the\ntime — that is luck, not process. Worth knowing that an isolated-worktree agent can still reach the\nshared checkout if its tooling is not scoped."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785800492578963001,"uuid":"0aea648a-f7ed-4af2-a208-cc219c648cc4"}